THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Anima-Engine depends on third-party components that remain governed by their own
licenses. Nothing in this file grants or restricts rights in those components.

A source distribution of this repository vendors no third-party code: every Rust
dependency is resolved by Cargo from crates.io and every JavaScript dependency by
npm, each carrying its own license text inside its own package.

A binary distribution (the Tauri desktop bundle from `npm run tauri:build`) does
carry them. Below are the direct dependencies of that build with the license each
one declares in its own manifest, read from `cargo metadata --features desktop`
and from `node_modules/*/package.json` on 2026-08-08:

  Rust — MIT OR Apache-2.0
    bevy_ecs, glam, rand, rand_chacha, rayon, serde, serde_json,
    crossbeam-channel, socket2, image, ureq, futures-util,
    burn, burn-ndarray, burn-wgpu (feature `ml-wgpu`)

  Rust — Apache-2.0 OR MIT
    tauri, tauri-plugin-shell, tauri-build, uuid

  Rust — Apache-2.0/MIT (dual, declared with the legacy separator)
    noise

  Rust — MIT
    tokio, bincode, dotenvy, ts-rs,
    neo4rs (feature `neo4j`), tokio-tungstenite (feature `networking`)

  JavaScript — MIT
    react, react-dom, pixi.js, three, @react-three/fiber

  JavaScript — Apache-2.0 OR MIT
    @tauri-apps/api

This list covers direct dependencies only; it is maintained by hand and is not a
generated, transitively complete inventory. That inventory is tracked as OSS-004
in docs/planning/OPEN_SOURCE_ADOPTION_PLAN.md. For the authoritative set as
built, run `cargo tree --features desktop` in src-tauri/ and `npm ls --omit=dev`
at the repository root.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPTIONAL EXTERNAL SERVICES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Neo4j is an optional runtime service, not a dependency of this software. With the
`neo4j` Cargo feature enabled, Anima-Engine talks to a separately installed Neo4j
server over the Bolt network protocol; without the feature, or when no server is
reachable, lineage falls back to an in-memory tracker. Neo4j Community Edition is
distributed under the GPLv3 by Neo4j, Inc. and is neither included in nor linked
into this software. Obtaining and licensing it is the operator's responsibility.
